  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)...\nThere may be some influx of monsoonal moisture in easterly flow\naloft into the mountains and deserts for Thursday through next \nweekend. High temperatures will change little or may decrease\nslightly in the lower deserts depending on the amount of any\nmoisture influx. Low temperatures will warm slightly. \n\nHigh temperatures for Thursday through Saturday will generally\nrange from a few degrees above average near the coast to 4 to 8\ndegrees above average for inland areas. High temperatures will\nrange from the mid 70s to lower 80s near the coast to the 90s to\n104 for the Inland Empire with 108 to 114 for the lower deserts.\n\nChances for measurable rainfall each afternoon for the mountains \nfrom showers or thunderstorms mostly less than 15 percent.",
